FACTORY_ACCEPTANCE_V1={"issue":5692,"head":"14f8d72a52318663386cdbc2e25d19f2e1b3e8a9","issue_digest":"be64e4cf380f1e479d3918e88d2013a0598d5559a6379be4ce84df7b7d98eb1f","items":[{"id":"A1","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ImageWithLoading.tsx, frontend/src/components/ComicIssueCard.tsx","evidence":"Root cause is frontend rendering/recycling: virtualized Queue rows recycled without remounting kept stale art or accepted late load/error events. Fix: ImageWithLoading remounts on source change via requestKey key, tracks imgRef/loadedImageRef/failedImageRef to ignore detached events, and settles cache hits via complete && naturalWidth > 0. ComicIssueCover remounts artwork via key JSON.stringify([coverImageUrl, threadTitle, issueNumber]).","test":"pnpm exec vitest run src/unit/ImageWithLoading.test.tsx src/unit/ComicIssueCard.test.tsx src/unit/QueueThreadCard.test.tsx -> 3 files passed, 104 tests passed"},{"id":"A2","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/pages/QueuePage/QueueThreadCard.tsx","evidence":"Copied page text shows cover labels but not whether browser received null URL/fetch failure. Investigation traced QueueThreadCard (lines 209-216) passing thread.series_cover_image_url into ComicIssueCover -> ImageWithLoading, confirming the rendering path is shared for eligible and blocked series.","test":"Code review of QueueThreadCard.tsx:209-216 and ComicIssueCard.tsx"},{"id":"A3","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/pages/QueuePage/QueueThreadCard.tsx","evidence":"Only FF is explicitly blocked in evidence; rows #29-#34 also affected with no blocker. Fix covers both: QueueThreadCard renders cover for all threads regardless of isBlocked (lines 209-216), and a dedicated test verifies a blocked series (FF) renders its cover while keeping blocker explanation and manual actions unchanged.","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx 'renders a blocked series cover without changing its prerequisite or manual actions'"},{"id":"A4","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/unit/QueueThreadCard.test.tsx","evidence":"Reported examples (#29-#35) are reproduction targets, not proof of valid covers. Tests cover covered, uncovered, blocked, failed-fetch, and far-down virtualized row cases matching the reported rows.","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx new tests: blocked series cover, failed cover -> No cover, changing cover, recycled row for blocked series"},{"id":"A5","status":"pass","file":"native/roll-service/src/threads.rs","evidence":"series_cover_image_url is null when no confirmed issue cover exists (threads.rs:117-118, SQL DISTINCT ON with WHERE ic.cover_url IS NOT NULL at lines 1261-1265). Frontend shows 'No cover' placeholder when url null/empty/failed (ComicIssueCoverArtwork). Never borrows art from another issue/series.","test":"native/roll-service/tests/thread_series_cover.rs"},{"id":"A6","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/pages/QueuePage/QueueThreadCard.tsx","evidence":"Behavior matches PR #5476 design: ComicIssueCover renders the provider CDN URL unchanged (no proxy/rewrite), fixed 2:3 frame via aspectRatio '2 / 3', lazy loading default, No cover placeholder when absent.","test":"ComicIssueCard.test.tsx 'keeps the provider URL unchanged, replaces broken art, and recovers on mapping change'"},{"id":"A7","status":"pass","file":"native/roll-service/src/threads.rs","evidence":"Set-based series_cover projection selects DISTINCT ON (thread_id) ordered by next_unread_issue_id first, then position, then issue_id (threads.rs:1261-1270), so the next unread confirmed covered issue wins, falling back to first confirmed covered issue by position.","test":"native/roll-service/tests/thread_series_cover.rs"},{"id":"A8","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ComicIssueCard.tsx","evidence":"When coverImageUrl is null/empty/failed, ComicIssueCoverArtwork renders the shared 'No cover' placeholder div with data-testid and aria-label 'No cover for <label>', never borrowing art from another issue/series.","test":"ComicIssueCard.test.tsx and QueueThreadCard.test.tsx 'replaces failed series art with No cover while preserving issue actions'"},{"id":"A9","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/pages/QueuePage/QueueThreadCard.tsx","evidence":"Blocked/eligible state (isBlocked, blocking_reasons) is computed by backend Option E and rendered separately (blocker tooltip at line 228-232). Cover rendering depends only on series_cover_image_url; blocked state does not gate cover.","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx blocked-series cover test confirms cover renders while blocker link and manual button remain"},{"id":"A10","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ImageWithLoading.tsx","evidence":"Fixed 2:3 footprint preserved via ComicIssueCover frame style aspectRatio '2 / 3'. Lazy loading default ('lazy') for compact Queue variant. No permanent spinner: cache-hit settles opacity-100 immediately; failed image shows placeholder (not spinner). No stale cover: remount on source change.","test":"ImageWithLoading.test.tsx cache-hit, lazy zero-width, and source-change tests; QueueThreadCard.test.tsx lazy/reveal tests"},{"id":"A11","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/pages/QueuePage/QueueThreadCard.tsx","evidence":"Tests cover scrolling/virtualization (recycled row test), revisiting loaded rows (source-change test), refresh (rerender), and desktop/mobile widths are layout-driven (no width-specific cover logic).","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx 'does not carry visible art into a replacement cover' and 'resets cover state when a far-down virtualized row is recycled for a blocked series'"},{"id":"A12","status":"pass","file":"native/roll-service/src/threads.rs","evidence":"series_cover_image_url is present in Rust v2 threads response: ThreadListItem field at line 118, populated from PageRow at line 799, assigned at line 868, and sourced from SQL cov.cover_url at line 1297. Field is present (not missing).","test":"Inspected threads.rs:118, 799, 868, 1297; openapi-thread-contract.test.ts asserts string|null|undefined type"},{"id":"A13","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ImageWithLoading.tsx","evidence":"Inspected component lifecycle: key-based remount on source change, imgRef tracks current element, handleLoad/handleError ignore detached events via loadedImageRef/failedImageRef refs, cache-hit detection via complete && naturalWidth > 0. Differentiates HTTP/CDN failures (onError -> placeholder) from lazy/virtualization (zero-width stays pending) from loaded-but-invisible (opacity-0 until load).","test":"ImageWithLoading.test.tsx: 'keeps a deferred lazy image pending when complete has zero intrinsic width', 'settles a cached successful image through onLoad exactly once', 'starts every changed source with fresh art and ignores detached request events'"},{"id":"A14","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ComicIssueCard.tsx","evidence":"Fixed at existing owner (ComicIssueCard/ImageWithLoading). Extracted ComicIssueCoverArtwork sub-component within ComicIssueCard.tsx (no parallel cover component). No client-side ComicVine search per row, no N+1 fetches, no image proxy, no CDN rewriting, no new cover-processing service.","test":"Diff review confirms only existing component files changed; no new services/components added"},{"id":"A15","status":"pass","file":"native/roll-service/src/threads.rs, frontend/src/pages/QueuePage/QueueThreadCard.tsx","evidence":"Queue order, thread ownership, issue identity, mapping confidence precedence (backend ORDER BY m.confidence DESC), read/rate actions, and Option E prerequisites all unchanged. No data repair or forced remapping.","test":"QueueThreadCard tests preserve Read/Rate/Map button enabled; backend threads.rs unchanged except cover projection already present"},{"id":"A16","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/unit/QueueThreadCard.test.tsx","evidence":"A confirmed covered next-unread issue produces the correct visible thumbnail: test renders thread with series_cover_image_url and asserts img src equals the cover URL, loading='lazy', then opacity-100 after fireEvent.load.","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx 'renders the derived series cover lazily and reveals it after loading'"},{"id":"A17","status":"pass","file":"native/roll-service/src/threads.rs","evidence":"Backend set-based fallback selects next unread confirmed covered issue first, then first confirmed covered issue by position (threads.rs:1261-1270), so the correct representative issue is used without selecting the wrong issue. Frontend displays whatever URL is provided.","test":"native/roll-service/tests/thread_series_cover.rs"},{"id":"A18","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/unit/QueueThreadCard.test.tsx","evidence":"Blocked series (FF waiting on Fantastic Four #600) renders its cover when a confirmed covered issue is available, while remaining blocked: test asserts cover image loads to opacity-100, blocker label present, Open Fantastic Four link shows 'Read Fantastic Four #600 first', and Read/Rate/Map button enabled.","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx 'renders a blocked series cover without changing its prerequisite or manual actions'"},{"id":"A19","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ComicIssueCard.tsx","evidence":"Series without valid confirmed cover shows 'No cover' placeholder (not alt text, broken image, permanent loading, or unrelated artwork). Existing mapping actions remain usable. Test asserts placeholder aria-label 'No cover for Failed Cover', no img, no status spinner, Read/Rate/Map button enabled.","test":"QueueThreadCard.test.tsx 'replaces failed series art with No cover while preserving issue actions'"},{"id":"A20","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/components/ImageWithLoading.tsx","evidence":"Images behave after scroll-in (lazy), virtualization/recycling (remount on key change), cache hits (complete && naturalWidth > 0 settles immediately), navigating away/back (fresh element), refreshing (rerender), slow/failed loads (error -> placeholder), and changed series never briefly shows previous art (fresh element per source).","test":"ImageWithLoading.test.tsx all new source-change/recycle/cache-hit tests; QueueThreadCard.test.tsx recycle test"},{"id":"A21","status":"pass","file":"native/roll-service/src/threads.rs","evidence":"Backend response unchanged: set-based series_cover projection (single SQL query, DISTINCT ON) already in place. No one-request-per-row behavior; no ComicPile-hosted image transformations (provider URL unchanged). Route/network budgets intact.","test":"native/roll-service/tests/thread_series_cover.rs; build + typecheck clean"},{"id":"A22","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/unit/ImageWithLoading.test.tsx, frontend/src/unit/ComicIssueCard.test.tsx, frontend/src/unit/QueueThreadCard.test.tsx","evidence":"Focused regression coverage added at the correct layer (frontend component tests, since the defect is display-side): covered, uncovered (No cover), blocked, failed-fetch, and far-down virtualized row cases. Backend projection already had thread_series_cover.rs.","test":"104 tests passed across 3 files (ImageWithLoading, ComicIssueCard, QueueThreadCard)"},{"id":"A23","status":"remaining","file":"/tmp/factory-review-findings-1398943891600-pr5737.md","evidence":"Requires verification in an authenticated deployed browser (production revision + representative images/requests for one ordinary row and one blocked row). Cannot be performed in this local agent environment (no production access/deployment). Not a code blocker: unit tests + lint + typecheck + build all pass.","test":"N/A - post-deploy production verification step; local gates (lint 0 errors, typecheck clean, build success, vitest 104 passed) are green"},{"id":"A24","status":"pass","file":"docs/manual-qa/queue.md","evidence":"#5433 broader cover-consistency epic remains open and separate; this ticket is a specific Queue regression fix, not a duplicate. No changes to #5433 scope needed.","test":"Docs/context review only"},{"id":"A25","status":"pass","file":"frontend/src/unit/QueueThreadCard.test.tsx, native/